        "id": 1758351
      },
      "writtenOn": "2026-10-06T10:49:05Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I think it is needed because it is part of netdev_ops now. If we ever want to backport anything to apf_ops (e.g. add new method based on upstream review feedback), We will need to use kabi_reserved slot for backport.\n\nSee detailed jetski analysis as follows:\n\n```\nit is tracked by STG because it is reachable from `register_netdev` via `dev-\u003enetdev_ops-\u003eapf_ops`, and its full definition is emitted in `gki/aarch64/abi.stg` (currently `bytesize: 128`).\n\nVendor Wi-Fi drivers implement `struct apf_ops`. The reserves allow adding new driver callbacks in future minor/LTS releases via `ANDROID_KABI_USE` without changing the struct size or breaking KMI (similar to `struct tlsdev_ops` in `include/net/tls.h`).\n```",
      "parentUuid": "0eba9ae2_566c77e3",
